{"request_sha256": "a97aec4ecf123800ce35e2b0cea14dd9d741b2aeba42c5b731c13a130b52555f", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "3ff90114caf64c906518728de44fcb45ec45c13a7fcfc4d6ba0e3a5fca0b675a", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7286}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["crown-pinnate-arching-fronds: in both P-WHOLE renders (render-0, render-1) the crown is a flat, nearly planar star of ~20-25 short, straight, needle-thin axes radiating from the apex. They do not arch outward-and-downward, no frond descends below the crown base, and the crown outline is a thin disc rather than the rounded hemisphere/shuttlecock of reference-0 and reference-1. Defining mismatch.", "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow: leaflets in render-0/render-1 read as a sparse dotted fringe of sub-pixel specks along each rachis; at P-TRUNK range (render-2) they resolve as tiny scattered green flecks with large gaps, not the dense, stiff, sharply tapering linear-lanceolate leaflets inserted in groups at differing angles that give the plumose V-section of reference-0/1/2. Leaflet size and density are a defining mismatch.", "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern: the rendered trunk in render-0, render-1 and the lit right-hand band of render-2 is a smooth, untextured tapering cylinder with no stubs, no spiral, no rhomboid lattice, against the coarse projecting diamond stub lattice of reference-1/reference-2 and the knobbly distance texture of reference-0. Absence is directly observable on the lit surface, not merely unresolved. (Owner scopes trunk organs to fn-110, not landed; recorded as an unmet core trait, not dismissed.)", "trunk-fibrous-matting: no fibre, husk or shaggy interstitial material anywhere on the rendered trunk in render-0/1/2; reference-1 and reference-2 show reddish-brown matting packing the lattice throughout. Unmet core trait (same fn-110 scope note).", "fruit-clusters-pendent: no inflorescence stalks or fruit bunches in render-0 or render-1; reference-0 shows two to three heavy pendent orange-red bunches emerging among the frond bases. Unmet core trait (owner scopes the date cluster to fn-111, not landed; recorded, not dismissed).", "owner-trunk-straight-constant: the trunk is visibly wavy in both seeds — render-0 carries at least three S-bends between the crown base and mid-trunk with a pronounced kink just below the crown; render-1 shows a sharp lateral jog roughly a third down from the crown plus lesser undulations. This is waviness in the silhouette, distinct from the straight or gently leaning posture the owner requires and from both the straight (reference-1/2) and smoothly S-leaning (reference-0) reference postures.", "P-BASE (render-3) is unusable as evidence: the frame is filled edge-to-edge by an unlit near-black trunk mass with no ground line, no leaf-base detail and no scale cue; the input also carries visibility "hidden". The leaf-base-close cell cannot be assessed either way."], "observations": ["Render framing: render-0 and render-1 place the tree small in frame with the crown occupying roughly the top sixth of the image; crown spread is on the order of 1.5-2x the visible crown-base width but only a small fraction of trunk length, whereas in reference-0 the crown spread is several times the trunk diameter and frond length is a substantial fraction of visible trunk length.", "The rendered stem is single and unbranched in every render view, with diameter roughly constant from just above the basal flare to the crown; a modest flare is present where it meets the ground in render-0/render-1.", "Nothing is attached to or emerging from the rendered trunk in any view — no epiphytes, no dead-frond skirt, no sprouts. The ferns and vines of reference-1/reference-2 are inventory-flagged as scene features rather than species character, and the owner requires a bare trunk; the render satisfies that requirement.", "Foliage colour in the renders is a mid-to-dark saturated green with near-black shaded facets; this sits inside the inventory's recorded colour range (deep green in reference-0 to grey-glaucous in reference-1/2) and is not treated as a mismatch.", "Finish quality against anchor-0 (spruce, stylistic floor only): the rendered palm's foliage renders as hard-edged specks with aliased silhouettes and large black self-shadowed regions, notably the crown in render-2 and the entire trunk in render-3, whereas the anchor presents evenly lit, coherent foliage mass. Recorded as a finish observation; the anchor carries no morphological weight.", "Between the two seeds the crown differs only slightly (render-1 shows marginally longer axes and a few more downward-tilted ones than render-0); neither reaches drooping. Seed variation does not change any cell verdict.", "The two references showing the trunk close up (reference-1, reference-2) are treated as independent specimens per the inventory; no core trunk trait was read from a single image alone except where the inventory itself cites one reference.", "Inventory statements were checked against the photographs rather than assumed; every core trait cited above was confirmed visible in the references named for it."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown reads as a thin flat star of short straight axes with no arching and no fronds drooping below the crown base, in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond length and leaflet size dials being set far below target, as the owner anticipates; the images do not establish any particular generator cause."}, {"observation": "Leaflets appear as sparse sub-pixel specks rather than dense stiff linear-lanceolate blades, even at the nearer P-TRUNK framing.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Trunk silhouette undulates with multiple visible bends and a kink below the crown in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner's note that the palm's taper value of 1.0 lies outside the authored 0.05-0.6 range points at trunk shaping parameters, but the renders alone do not confirm this."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface is smooth and bare: no leaf-base stubs, no spiral lattice, no fibrous matting, on the lit portion of the close view as well as at whole-tree scale.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states trunk organs (fn-110) are not landed; this is consistent with, but not proven by, the images."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunches anywhere in the rendered crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states the date cluster (fn-111) is not landed."}, {"observation": "A single unbranched stem of roughly constant diameter carries the crown, with a modest basal flare and no foliage on the trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The P-BASE view is a full-frame unlit black mass with no resolvable surface, and its input is marked visibility "hidden"; the leaf-base close-range cell is unassessable.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Camera placement inside or hard against the trunk with the subject facing away from the light would produce this; no mechanism is established."}, {"observation": "Rendered foliage colour falls within the inventory's recorded green-to-glaucous range.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No dead-frond skirt, no orange petiole-base sheath, and no basal leaflet spines are present in the renders; these are secondary refinements in the inventory, not defining reference character.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Crown-to-trunk proportion is far smaller in the renders than in reference-0, but the inventory records this ratio as unmeasurable and view-dependent, so it is reported alongside the frond-length blocker rather than as a separate defining failure.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Foliage edges are aliased and large regions of both crown and trunk fall to near-black, below the even, coherent finish of the spruce anchor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "anchor-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "References show 30-60 long once-pinnate fronds arching outward and downward into a hemispherical/shuttlecock crown with recurved older fronds. Renders show ~20-25 short, straight, thin axes in a nearly planar star; none recurve or descend below the crown base. Defining mismatch in both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Reference leaflets are narrow, stiff, sharply tapering, densely inserted in groups at differing angles giving a plumose V-sectioned frond with a bristly margin. Rendered leaflets are isolated specks along a bare rachis with wide gaps and no discernible grouping or V-section, at both whole and trunk framing."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Reference trunks are clothed in projecting wedge-shaped leaf-base stubs tessellating into a spiral diamond lattice. The rendered trunk is a smooth untextured cylinder; the lit right-hand band of render-2 shows the surface clearly enough to confirm absence rather than non-resolution. Owner scopes this to fn-110 (not landed) — recorded as unmet, not dismissed."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Reference-1 and reference-2 show coarse reddish-brown fibre and shredded husk packing the interstices of the stub lattice. No fibre, husk or shaggy layer appears anywhere on the rendered trunk. Same fn-110 scope note; recorded as unmet."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "A single unbranched stem of roughly constant diameter carries the crown in every render view, with no branching at any height — matching the references. The trunk's waviness is a separate owner-priority failure and does not negate the solitary unbranched columnar character recorded by this trait."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Reference-0 shows two to three dense pendent orange-red fruit bunches on thick downward-bending stalks emerging among the frond bases. No inflorescence, stalk or fruit mass appears in either render. Owner scopes the date cluster to fn-111 (not landed) — recorded as unmet core trait, not dismissed or downgraded."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary trait. Reference-0 shows a brown-to-grey collar of dead fronds collapsed against the upper trunk below the living crown. Absent in both renders. Refinement, not a blocker."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, itself flagged uncertain in the inventory. Rendered foliage is a mid-to-dark saturated green, inside the deep-green to grey-glaucous span recorded across the references. Acceptable variation."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary trait. The rendered crown apex in render-2 is largely in black self-shadow and the leaf bases are not separately resolvable at whole-tree framing; presence or absence of pale petioles with rust-orange sheath material cannot be judged."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait spanning vertical-and-straight (reference-1/2) to a single smooth S-lean with swollen basal curve (reference-0). The rendered trunk is near-vertical but carries multiple short-wavelength bends and a kink below the crown in both seeds — outside the recorded range and contrary to the owner's explicit 'never wavy' requirement."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait; the inventory records the ferns and vines as scene features present only in reference-1/2 and absent in reference-0. The rendered trunk bears nothing, which is within the recorded range and matches the owner's bare-trunk requirement."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary trait. References show grey-brown to warm reddish-brown with lighter bleached stub faces against darker fibre. The rendered trunk is a flat dark brown gradient with no tonal variation, and in render-2/render-3 collapses to near-black over most of its width. Finish refinement, not a defining blocker."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary trait, inventory-flagged uncertain. A modest widening where the trunk meets the ground is visible in both P-WHOLE renders, consistent with the broad rooted base of reference-0 at the coarse level the reference supports. No root-boss detail is required or claimed."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary trait. No smooth green crownshaft appears in the renders; the frond bases sit directly on the trunk, as in reference-1. Note this passes trivially while the stub covering that should occupy that surface is itself missing."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary trait, inventory-flagged uncertain even in the references. The proximal ends of the rendered fronds are lost in crown shadow in render-2 and unresolvable in render-0/1; the presence of reduced spine-like structures cannot be assessed."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation trait, inventory-flagged unmeasurable. Even allowing for viewing distance, the rendered crown spread is a small multiple of trunk width and frond length is a minor fraction of trunk length, against a crown spread several times trunk width and substantial frond-to-trunk length ratio in reference-0. Reported here as a symptom of the frond-length blocker rather than an independent defining failure."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"1c9546ed-1fa5-45e0-bbcb-84b503676df1","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySource":"none","claude_code_version":"2.1.278","output_style":"default","agents":["claude","Explore","general-purpose","Plan"],"skills":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator"],"plugins":[{"name":"flow-next","path":"/home/daniel/.claude-profiles/danithekiller93/plugins/cache/flow-next/flow-next/6.0.0","source