{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfJjrAesiRwNqibD3JV7t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kyiqd8Y69RMTp5NNgZArQW","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"passes":["fail","fail","fail","unknown","fail","fail","fail","fail","pass","pass"],"defects":["crown-pinnate-arching-fronds: in both P-WHOLE renders (render-0, render-1) the crown is a flat, nearly planar star of ~20-25 short, straight, needle-thin axes radiating from the apex. They do not arch outward-and-downward, no frond descends below the crown base, and the crown outline is a thin disc rather than the rounded hemisphere/shuttlecock of reference-0 and reference-1. Defining mismatch.","leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow: leaflets in render-0/render-1 read as a sparse dotted fringe of sub-pixel specks along each rachis; at P-TRUNK range (render-2) they resolve as tiny scattered green flecks with large gaps, not the dense, stiff, sharply tapering linear-lanceolate leaflets inserted in groups at differing angles that give the plumose V-section of reference-0/1/2. Leaflet size and density are a defining mismatch.","trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern: the rendered trunk in render-0, render-1 and the lit right-hand band of render-2 is a smooth, untextured tapering cylinder with no stubs, no spiral, no rhomboid lattice, against the coarse projecting diamond stub lattice of reference-1/reference-2 and the knobbly distance texture of reference-0. Absence is directly observable on the lit surface, not merely unresolved. (Owner scopes trunk organs to fn-110, not landed; recorded as an unmet core trait, not dismissed.)","trunk-fibrous-matting: no fibre, husk or shaggy interstitial material anywhere on the rendered trunk in render-0/1/2; reference-1 and reference-2 show reddish-brown matting packing the lattice throughout. Unmet core trait (same fn-110 scope note).","fruit-clusters-pendent: no inflorescence stalks or fruit bunches in render-0 or render-