s; this sits inside the inventory's recorded colour range (deep green in reference-0 to grey-glaucous in reference-1/2) and is not treated as a mismatch.","Finish quality against anchor-0 (spruce, stylistic floor only): the rendered palm's foliage renders as hard-edged specks with aliased silhouettes and large black self-shadowed regions, notably the crown in render-2 and the entire trunk in render-3, whereas the anchor presents evenly lit, coherent foliage mass. Recorded as a finish observation; the anchor carries no morphological weight.","Between the two seeds the crown differs only slightly (render-1 shows marginally longer axes and a few more downward-tilted ones than render-0); neither reaches drooping. Seed variation does not change any cell verdict.","The two references showing the trunk close up (reference-1, reference-2) are treated as independent specimens per the inventory; no core trunk trait was read from a single image alone except where the inventory itself cites one reference.","Inventory statements were checked against the photographs rather than assumed; every core trait cited above was confirmed visible in the references named for it."],"findings":[{"observation":"Crown reads as a thin flat star of short straight axes with no arching and no fronds drooping below the crown base, in both seeds.","evidence_ids":["render-0","render-1","reference-0","reference-1"],"impact":"blocker","uncertain":false,"causal_hypothesis":"Consistent with frond length and leaflet size dials being set far below target, as the owner anticipates; the images do not establish any particular generator cause."},{"observation":"Leaflets appear as sparse sub-pixel specks rather than dense stiff linear-lanceolate blades, even at the nearer P-TRUNK framing.","evidence_ids":["render-0","render-1","render-2","reference-0","reference-1","reference-2"],"impact":"blocker","uncertain":false,"causal_hypothesis":null},{"observation":"Trunk silhouette undulates with multiple visible bends 